description:
Design a 32-bit modulo operation circuit that computes the remainder of the division of input `a` by input `b`. If the divisor `b` is zero, the circuit outputs zero to avoid division by zero errors; otherwise, it outputs the result of `a % b`. The remainder is provided as a 32-bit output `r`.
module top_module(
  input [31:0] a,
  input [31:0] b,
  output reg [31:0] r
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [31:0] a,
  input [31:0] b,
  output reg [31:0] r
);// Inputs
// a: dividend, b: divisor
// Outputs
// r: remainder

// Verilog code for modulo operator
always @(*) begin
  if (b == 0) begin
    r <= 0;
  end else begin
    r <= a % b;
  end
end

endmodule

